[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-039
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Armed rows
STATEMENT: >>>
`_armed_rows` sorts the frame by `timestamp` and keeps the rows inside the armed windows. When the log has no
arming data and the named solution column is present, it also drops every row before the first row whose
solution value is finite and has bit 0 (attitude) set; when no row has it, all rows are kept.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-040
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Flag columns
STATEMENT: >>>
`_bits` returns `(None, None)` when the column is absent or has one or no non-null value, so that check is not
run. Otherwise it returns the non-null values as 64-bit integers with their timestamps; rows with a null flag
are left out, not read as all bits clear.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test supplies a flags column with missing values. Inspection checks `_bits` and that each caller tests for
None.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-041
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EKF inputs, ratio source and skip
STATEMENT: >>>
`EKFAnalyser.analyse` takes the armed rows of `estimator_status` (solution column `solution_status_flags`) and
of `ekf_test_ratios` (solution column `solution_status`, else `flags`), ignoring a topic with no `timestamp`.
The ratio table is `estimator_innovation_test_ratios` limited to armed time when that topic has a `timestamp`;
else `estimator_status` when it has a column ending `_test_ratio`; else `ekf_test_ratios`. When each of the
three has fewer than 2 rows it returns `_skip("No EKF status samples <phase>.")`. Otherwise it returns an
assessed result, also when none of the columns it checks is present or every checked value is NaN; the result
is then 100.0 with no findings.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests check the ratio topic, the `estimator_status` ratios and `ekf_test_ratios` used alone. The skip and the
assessed result with nothing checked are found by inspection; no test drives them.
<<<
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-042
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Innovation check flags
STATEMENT: >>>
For each bit 0 to 12 of `innovation_check_flags` set in any armed sample `_innov_flags` adds one finding of
`kind` `ekf.innovation_rejected` titled "EKF Innovation Failure: <label>" (0 Horizontal Velocity, 1 Vertical
Velocity, 2 Horizontal Position, 3 Vertical Position, 4 to 6 Magnetometer X/Y/Z, 7 Yaw, 8 Airspeed, 9 Synthetic
Sideslip, 10 Height Above Ground, 11 and 12 Optical Flow X/Y). It is a warning with penalty 15 when the longest
run of set samples lasts `SUSTAINED_FAILURE_S` = 0.5 s or more, else info with penalty 5. A run lasts from its
first sample to the next sample after it. The time window runs from the start of the first run to the end of the
last.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-043
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Solution validity bits
STATEMENT: >>>
`_solution_flags` judges bit 0 (Attitude) and bit 5 (Vertical Position, Absolute) over all armed samples, and
bits 1 (Horizontal Velocity), 2 (Vertical Velocity), 3 (Horizontal Position, Relative) and 4 (Horizontal
Position, Absolute) only from the first sample where the bit is set, skipping a bit that is never set. When the
bit is clear in `INVALID_MIN_FRACTION` = 0.01 or more of the judged samples it adds a warning of `kind`
`ekf.solution_invalid` with penalty 15 and `confidence(fraction / 0.1 - 1, longest run in s)`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-044
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPS glitch and accelerometer error bits by source
STATEMENT: >>>
`_solution_flags` adds a warning of `kind` `ekf.gps_glitch` (penalty 15) when the glitch bit is set in any armed
sample and a critical finding of `kind` `ekf.accel_error` (penalty 30) when the accelerometer-error bit is set
in any armed sample, each with `confidence(episodes / 3, longest run in s)`. `EKFAnalyser.analyse` passes glitch
bit 10 and accelerometer bit 11 for `estimator_status.solution_status_flags`; glitch bit 14 and no accelerometer
bit for `ekf_test_ratios.solution_status`; and for `ekf_test_ratios.flags` (used only when `solution_status` is
absent) bits 10 and 11 when the autopilot is `"px4"`, else glitch bit 15 and no accelerometer bit, which is
also what an unknown autopilot gets.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-045
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ArduPilot filter faults
STATEMENT: >>>
For each bit 0 to 7 of `fault_status` set in any armed sample `_ap_faults` adds a finding of `kind`
`ekf.filter_fault`: critical with penalty 30 for bit 0 (attitude NaN) and bit 1 (velocity NaN); warning with
penalty 15 for bits 2 to 4 (bad magnetometer X/Y/Z), 5 (bad airspeed), 6 (bad sideslip) and 7 (filter not
initialised). Confidence is `confidence(episodes / 3, longest run in s)`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-046
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ArduPilot measurement timeouts
STATEMENT: >>>
For bits 0 (Position), 1 (Velocity), 2 (Height) and 3 (Magnetometer) of `timeout_status` `_ap_timeouts` skips a
bit that is set in every armed sample, judges from the first sample where it is clear, and adds a warning of
`kind` `ekf.sensor_timeout` with penalty 15 when the longest run of set samples lasts 0.5 s or more. Bits 4
(airspeed) and 5 (drag) are not judged.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Ratio columns
STATEMENT: >>>
`_ratio_groups` takes every column of the ratio table whose name does not start with `timestamp` and matches
`RATIO_COL`: a name starting with `gps`, `ev`, `rng`, `baro`, `aux`, `flow`, `heading`, `mag`, `gravity`,
`drag`, `airspeed`, `beta` or `hagl` followed by lower-case letters, digits or underscores and an optional
`[n]`, or a lower-case name ending `_test_ratio`. Columns that differ only in `[n]` are merged into one series
by the element-wise larger value, ignoring NaN. Any other column is ignored.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Test ratio above 1.0
STATEMENT: >>>
For each ratio series with a value above `RATIO_REJECT` = 1.0 `_innov_ratios` adds a finding of `kind`
`ekf.innovation_ratio` titled "EKF Innovation Ratio Exceeded: <label>": a warning with penalty 15 when the
longest run above 1.0 lasts 0.5 s or more, else info with penalty 5, with `confidence(peak - 1, longest)`, the
longest run as its time window and its own chart (`timestamps`, `ratio`, `col`, at most 500 points). A series
with any value above 1.0 is not passed to `_near_limit`. NaN values count as not above the limit.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-049
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Test ratio near the limit
STATEMENT: >>>
For a ratio series with no value above 1.0 `_near_limit` returns a warning of `kind`
`ekf.innovation_ratio_high` (penalty 10 added by the caller) when the longest run above `RATIO_NEAR` = 0.64
lasts `NEAR_LIMIT_MIN_S` = 2.0 s or more, with `confidence(peak / 0.64 - 1, longest)`; otherwise None. The same
limit applies to PX4 and ArduPilot ratios.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-050
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Wind jump
STATEMENT: >>>
When `estimator_status` has the columns `wind_vel_n` or `wind[0]` and `wind_vel_e` or `wind[1]`, `_wind` takes
the wind speed as the hypotenuse of the two and adds one warning of `kind` `ekf.wind_jump` with penalty 10 when
the absolute change between two consecutive armed samples is above `WIND_CHANGE_THRESH` = 5.0 m/s at least once,
whatever the time between the samples. Confidence is `confidence(biggest / 5.0 - 1)`; the window runs from the
first jump to the sample after the last.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: analysers
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-DYN-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-DYN-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: EKF module score
STATEMENT: >>>
`EKFAnalyser.analyse` starts `health_score` at 100.0 and subtracts the summed penalties of each group limited to
a cap: innovation flags 60.0; `estimator_status` solution flags 45.0; `ekf_test_ratios` solution flags 45.0;
filter faults 45.0; timeouts 30.0; test ratios 30.0; wind 10.0. The result carries the score limited to not
below 0.0.
<<<
