`EKFAnalyser.analyse` writes the key metric `max_innovation_ratio` (highest finite value over all ratio series,
4 places) when a series has a finite value, and no key metric otherwise. A finding without its own chart gets
`{"timestamps": ms, "innov_ratios": {series: values}}` downsampled to at most 500 points, or the timestamps of
the first table with 2 or more rows and an empty `innov_ratios` when there are no ratio series.
